# robonix/system/scene/go_to — take the robot to something named, or say
# which of several was meant.
#
# The whole operation, not a fragment of one. Before this, reaching an object
# meant list_objects → pick → goal_near → navigate, with the caller carrying
# a pose between the last two steps; with eight chairs in the room the
# picking step had nothing to pick on and chose one anyway.
#
# Scene resolves the reference itself (see robonix/system/scene/find),
# computes the approach pose, and calls robonix/service/navigation/navigate.
# Advertised only while that navigation capability is reachable: a contract
# that cannot do what it says should not be offered.

# What to go to, described the way a person would. Same fields as find.
string text
string cls
string region
RelationConstraint[] relations
string predicate
# Skip resolution entirely and go to this object. Use when acting on a
# choice a person already confirmed.
string object_id
# Answering a previous go_to that came back needs_clarification: the query it
# returned, and which candidate was chosen.
string query_id
string chosen_object_id
# Try the next candidate when navigation fails on the first. 0 → service
# default (2). Perception is not accurate enough for one attempt to be the
# whole answer.
int32 max_attempts
---
# arrived | unreachable | needs_clarification | nav_offline | not_found
string status
# What it went to, when it went somewhere.
string object_id
string label
# Where it stopped, in the map frame.
float64 x
float64 y
float64 yaw
# When needs_clarification: the candidates and a question naming what
# separates them. Ask it; do not pick.
Candidate[] candidates
string question
# Hand back with the chosen object to continue without re-resolving. The
# scene moves, so resolving twice can produce a different set than the one
# the person was shown.
string query_id
# Which candidates were tried and why each failed, when it did.
string[] attempts
string detail
